<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Colony of Jamaica</h1><p class="st-meta">1655 CE – 1962 CE · capital Spanish Town; later Kingston</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Britain's most valuable Caribbean colony for much of the 18th century, a sugar island built on slavery that became independent in 1962.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>An English expedition under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sir-william-penn">William Penn</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-venables">Robert Venables</a>, part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oliver-cromwell">Oliver Cromwell's</a> Western Design, failed against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santo-domingo">Santo Domingo</a> and seized lightly defended <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/spanish-jamaica">Spanish Jamaica</a> in 1655. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> ceded the island by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-madrid-1670">Treaty of Madrid</a> in 1670. Port Royal, base of buccaneers such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-morgan">Henry Morgan</a>, flourished until an earthquake destroyed it in 1692.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>A governor ruled with an elected planter assembly, from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-town">Spanish Town</a> until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingston-jamaica">Kingston</a> became capital in 1872. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">Sugar</a> estates using enslaved Africans made <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/jamaica">Jamaica</a> enormously profitable. Resistance was constant, from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tackys-revolt">Tacky's Revolt</a> of 1760 to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baptist-war">Baptist War</a> of 1831 to 1832 led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samuel-sharpe">Samuel Sharpe</a>, which hastened emancipation in 1834 to 1838. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morant-bay-rebellion">Morant Bay rebellion</a> of 1865 the assembly was abolished and crown colony rule imposed.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Labour unrest in 1938 gave rise to trade unions and parties led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-bustamante">Alexander Bustamante</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norman-manley">Norman Manley</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/universal-suffrage">Universal suffrage</a> came in 1944. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/jamaica">Jamaica</a> joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/west-indies-federation">West Indies Federation</a> in 1958 but left after a 1961 referendum and became independent as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamaica">Jamaica</a> on 6 August 1962.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/colony-of-jamaica.jpg" alt="Colony of Jamaica" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Thommy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Jamaica_(1957%E2%80%931962).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1655 CE – 1962 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Spanish Town; later Kingston</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Henry Morgan, Edward John Eyre</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Protestantism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English and Jamaican Patois</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/jamaica">Jamaica</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>British Jamaica</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1808&amp;focus=colony-of-jamaica" aria-label="Colony of Jamaica on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2597 1510 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Colony of Jamaica lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M2917 1766L4997 651M2917 1766L2901 1759M2917 1766L3305 2036M2917 1766L2917 1767M2917 1766L2892 1757M2917 1766L3090 1640M2917 1766L2800 1719"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4997 651h0M2901 1759h0M3305 2036h0M2917 1767h0M2892 1757h0M3090 1640h0M2800 1719h0"/><